- **Dioxus DOM bridge:** DOM events route to the vdom via the nearest `data-dioxus-id` attribute parsed as `usize` (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:47-55; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:411-417); listener registration sets a `"<rust func>"` placeholder and `data-dioxus-id` (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/mutation_writer.rs:338-345); `__webview_document` sets a sub-document and `data` on `<object>` a custom widget (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/mutation_writer.rs:248-284); `style`-namespace attributes become style properties and `dangerous_inner_html` sets inner HTML (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/mutation_writer.rs:402-437); a falsy value (Bool false, Text `"false"`, Int 0, Float 0.0, None) of one of the 28 names of upstream's private predicate `is_bool_attr`, a closed `matches!` set — `allowfullscreen`, `allowpaymentrequest`, `async`, `autofocus`, `autoplay`, `checked`, `controls`, `default`, `defer`, `disabled`, `formnovalidate`, `hidden`, `ismap`, `itemscope`, `loop`, `multiple`, `muted`, `nomodule`, `novalidate`, `open`, `playsinline`, `readonly`, `required`, `reversed`, `selected`, `truespeed`, `webkitdirectory` and `inert` — the 27 names before `inert` the module-private `BOOLEAN_ATTRIBUTES` list of escher's own, retired at 2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship for upstream's predicate (#1188), which left `mutation_writer.rs` byte-identical to upstream's at `434e0661` — clears the attribute, on the dynamic and the static template attribute path alike; a truthy value of a listed name is still written, and an attribute outside the list holding `false` (`aria-hidden`, a `data-` attribute) is still written as `"false"`; a framework-written `inert: false` is cleared and leaves content as it was, while a truthy `inert` makes its subtree inert
 — not focusable, not hit, out of the accessibility tree and the snapshot (§Established Decisions → DOM semantics); so an element rendered `hidden: false` carries no `hidden` attribute, is laid out and is a snapshot node, and one rendered with a truthy `hidden` is excluded (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/mutation_writer.rs:439-475; tests/blitz-tests/tests/dioxus_falsy_boolean_attrs.rs:1-8) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-snapshot-state-fidelity/report.md and, for the 28-name predicate, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship/report.md; `SubDocumentAttr` / `CustomWidgetAttr` write-once, compared by id (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/write_once_attr.rs:6-70); event converter for form, mouse, keyboard, focus, mounted, pointer, scroll, touch, wheel (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/events.rs:42-138); `NodeHandle` backs `MountedData` (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/events.rs:195-307); `DioxusDocument` exposes `vdom`, `inner`, `vdom_state.try_element_to_node_id(ElementId)` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:66; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:76-80); **stable element ids** — `DioxusDocument::element_id(NodeId) -> Option<String>` (`None` for a non-element, stale or detached node, never panics) and `element_ids() -> Vec<(NodeId, String)>` (every element reachable from the document root, document pre-order, ids pairwise distinct) compute the id on demand from a vdom walk joined with a DOM walk and write it to neither the DOM nor the vdom (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:198-230; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:186-282); the id is one of four tiers, in order of precedence — (1) the **author key** — the HTML `id` verbatim when non-empty, `/`-free and the first in document pre-order to claim it — else (2) the **anchored path**
 — for an element under an element of its own component instance that reads an author key: that key, `//`, then one element segment per DOM level below the keyed element (`box//p:0/b:0`), the nearest such keyed element anchoring — else (3) the **component path** — `/`-joined component segments below the app root, where dioxus-core's four framework scopes (`ScopeId::ROOT` · `ROOT_SUSPENSE_BOUNDARY` · `ROOT_ERROR_BOUNDARY` · `APP`, the user root dioxus-core names `"root"`) add none, a segment is the last `::` segment of `VComponent.name` (dioxus-core's full type path) with generics stripped, and an owner's 2nd and later instance of one name reads `{name}:{k}`, then one element segment per DOM level, `{tag}[{key}]` for a template root of a Dioxus-keyed VNode (non-empty, `/`-free, first among its siblings) else `{tag}:{n}` with `n` the index among same-parent, same-owner-instance, same-tag element siblings; a template root owned by its DOM parent's owner (a list row, an `if` branch) continues the parent's path — the parent's own path, or `{key}/` when the parent reads its author key, which is what spells the anchored tier's `//` — one owned by another component restarts at that component's chain whatever keyed element it sits under, so an anchor acts inside one component only (`div#slot { Item {} }` leaves Item's root at `Item/b:0`), and the app root's own elements read `/{tag}:{n}…` — else (4) the **document path** of an element no component renders, `/` then `{tag}:{n}` per DOM level from the document root (`/html:0/body:0`); an `id` that fails the author-key predicate (empty, `/`-bearing, a later duplicate) anchors nothing, and the skeleton's `main` reads its key yet anchors nothing in a Dioxus app, its children being another owner's template roots; no id of one tier equals an id of another
 — an author key holds no `/`, and an anchored path is the only id holding `//`, a component path being non-empty names and segments and a document or app-root path starting with one `/` with no empty segment after it — so a key spelled like a component name stays distinct (`Item//b:0` beside `Item/b:0`); the anchored tier, its `key//segment` spelling and its one-component reach are ratified by the founder (2026-10-06) (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:44-58; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:78-161; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:208-214; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:225-270); no `NodeId`, `ElementId`, `ScopeId` or pointer enters an id; the id **holds across code edits** on the stand, in both layout modes — every element of each lean task reads the same id under an edited shell (an earlier sibling of the task root's tag, a wrapper around the task, one more level), every element that reads an author key under a same-tag sibling added before it, a sibling removed and a wrapped ancestor, every anchored element under an edit outside its keyed element, and every element under an edit of text, an attribute, a class or a handler — while an earlier same-tag sibling or a wrapper inserted between an unkeyed element and the point its path starts at changes that element's id and no keyed element's (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_id_edits.rs:1-6) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-id-stability-across-code-edits/report.md; on the stand the chrome reads its author keys (`main`, `task-shell`, `back-btn` …), the task root `TaskShell/Counter/div:0`, a CRUD row its author key `crud-person-0` and Home's seven cards `task-card-{slug}` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_element_ids.rs:130-256;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_actionable_keys.rs:85-105), each card's five children reading anchored paths (`task-card-counter//div:1/h2:0`) and no lean-task element reading one at boot — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-id-stability-across-code-edits/report.md; a node a re-render removes is dropped with its descendants by the bridge's crate-private `remove_and_drop_node` / `replace_and_drop_node`, their `element_id_mapping` / `node_id_mapping` entries cleared, so it no longer resolves and reads no id — `get_node` `None`, `element_id` `None`, no pair in `element_ids()` (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/mutation_writer.rs:110-130; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/element_id.rs:397-423) — upstream #1185, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-13-upstream-sync-polish-and-ship/report.md; until that chunk it was DETACHED (parent `None`) and kept resolving until its ElementId was reassigned, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-stable-element-ids/report.md; the id **persists** on the stand, in both layout modes and on each lean task: every element present before and after a re-render reads the same id; a remount (the task's card → Back → the same card in `app::app`) reads the same id list in order, equal to `stand::boot`'s, on fresh `NodeId`s for every element except the four document-skeleton elements `DioxusDocument::new` builds outside the VirtualDom (`/html:0`, `/html:0/head:0`, `/html:0/body:0`, `main`), and every dropped pre-remount `NodeId` reads `None`; a second process reads the same id lists (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:119-144; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_id_persistence.rs:1-3);
 the lean CRUD row's Dioxus key is its person's model-assigned `u64` (`key: "{person.id}"`, fixture people 0–2, Create from 3), set on the `for` item itself with the filter in the iterator, so the list diffs by key, and the row carries `id: "crud-person-{person.id}"` beside that key, so a row's id is its author key `crud-person-{person.id}` (fixture `crud-person-0..2`, Create from `crud-person-3`) and follows its person under filter, Create and Delete — a `key:` on an element inside an `if` within a `for` body does not key the list, whose items are then diffed by position (examples/seven_guis/src/tasks/crud.rs:92-108) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-id-persistence/report.md; under the `accessibility` feature `DioxusDocument` overrides `Document::accessibility_tree`: it builds the base tree, maps `element_ids()` by `NodeId::as_u64()` and sets each element node's AccessKit `author_id` to that element's stable id, while `TextRun`s, the document root and the synthetic `Window` (`u64::MAX`) carry none and no tree id indexes the slab — so the id reaches the accessibility tree the harness reads and the platform tree the shell builds, and is written to neither the DOM nor the vdom (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:310-326; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_accessibility_ids.rs:1-4); dioxus-native-dom's `accessibility` feature reads `["blitz-dom/accessibility", "dep:accesskit"]` and dioxus-native's `accessibility` forwards to it, so a crate taking either Dioxus crate with `default-features = false` (the workspace pin) gets the override, the snapshot model, its text form, its diff and the actionable-key check only by naming the feature or by depending on a crate that names it — blitz-tests and, since 2026-10-07-act-by-id, escher-driver name it on dioxus-native-dom;
 seven_guis names none in its own manifest and gets it through its `escher-driver` edge, so both its binaries compile these modules, with no platform adapter (packages/dioxus-native-dom/Cargo.toml:18; packages/dioxus-native/Cargo.toml:32; tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:21; packages/escher-driver/Cargo.toml:15) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-accessibility-tree-identity/report.md; under the same feature `DioxusDocument::snapshot(&self) -> Snapshot` reads the screen as a tree, read-only: it builds from that `accessibility_tree` override and walks its `children` lists from `TreeInfo.root`; `Snapshot { roots: Vec<SnapshotNode> }` offers `nodes()` (pre-order) and `get(&str)` (by stable element id), a `SnapshotNode` carries `id: String`, `role: accesskit::Role`, `name: String`, `state: NodeState`, `bounds: blitz_dom::BoundingRect` and `children`, and `NodeState` carries seven fields in the order `enabled: Option<bool>` · `checked: Option<bool>` · `value: Option<String>` · `selected: Option<bool>` · `pressed: Option<bool>` · `invalid: bool` · `focused: bool` — four until 2026-10-10-snapshot-states added the three after `value`, with no new public type, so a struct literal without a spread names all seven (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:63-74) — all three `Debug`, `Clone` and `PartialEq`, re-exported from the crate, together with the public constant `MASKED_VALUE: &str` (eight U+2022 characters), and through dioxus-native's `pub use dioxus_native_dom::*`; a node is a tree node carrying an `author_id` whose element resolves through `BaseDocument::get_node` — the `Window`, the document root and `TextRun`s are not nodes, their kept descendants attach to the nearest kept ancestor, generic containers are kept, and what the accessibility tree excludes never appears; every field is an existing reader's
 — `id` the `author_id` verbatim, `role` the node's `role()`, `name` its non-empty `label` else the concatenated names of its `labelled_by` targets (cycle-guarded, trimmed, `""` with no source) — since the 2026-10-17 upstream sync the `label` is also the computed text of an element's `aria-labelledby` targets, which outranks a `<label>` (§Standard Contracts → Mutation, query and CSSOM), while the snapshot reads no description and its `enabled` still reads the `disabled` attribute, so `aria-disabled` moves no snapshot reading (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:51-52; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:167) —, `bounds` `BaseDocument::get_client_bounding_rect` (viewport-relative, unclamped, for every element — an element under a transform read where its transforms move it (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18; the Scrolling, selection, tree contract), so a driver `click` on a translated button is accepted and lands (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_transformed.rs:81-193) — a box that is itself scrolled included since 2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit: the reader positions a node through the crate-private `BaseDocument::physical_unrounded_geometry`, which subtracts the scroll offset of every box on the containing-block chain above the node and not the node's own, in both of its bodies, so such a box reads the rect it stands at, the same before and after its content is scrolled, a scrolled box inside a scrolled box moves by the outer offset alone, and a step that scrolls a box does not name it among its changed nodes — on the stand `crud-list` reads the same four figures after its content is scrolled (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:2537-2567; the reader's two bodies, packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:2507-2534 without the `writing-mode` feature and packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/writing_mode.rs:371-412 with it;
 `offset_rect` and `inline_fragment_rects`, which take a box as their content's origin, apply that box's scroll offset themselves and answer as before; tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrolled_box_client_rect.rs:134-215, read under the per-package and the workspace build — fixed on the founder's ruling of 2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed by the overseer; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit/report.md); a scrolled box under a vertical writing mode, the vertical-chain path of the second body, is read since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep — a `writing-mode: vertical-lr` box scrolled (70, 120) reads its unscrolled rect (40, 50, 300, 200), green under the per-package and the workspace build, tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrolled_box_client_rect.rs:163-185), `enabled` the `disabled`-presence reading on a `can_be_disabled()` element — the reading that decides whether a click acts, so a `disabled="false"` and a bare `disabled` both read `Some(false)` and, since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, are not focusable either — the engine's focusability reader keys on presence too (§Established Decisions → DOM semantics; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:618-619) —, `checked` `checkbox_input_checked()` for a native checkbox or radio, else, for a node whose tree role is one of the five checkable roles (the snapshot's own private `is_checkable`, a copy of blitz-dom's), `toggled == Toggled::True` — `None` where the role states nothing, a mixed one `Some(false)` (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:170-182; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:220-232), `value` a `select`'s chosen option's value (`BaseDocument::select_value`, below), else the editor text, else — for a range `input`, since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction
 — its current value `range_input_value()`, the formatted value a key or a pointerdown moved while its `value` attribute keeps what the markup wrote (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:59-60; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:255-257; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:277-279), else the `value` attribute of a `textarea` or a text-entry `input`, except that a password `input` or a file `input` (the `type` compared ASCII-case-insensitively) reads `MASKED_VALUE` where that reading is non-empty and `""` where it is empty (a file input with no `value` attribute reads `None`), never the text, its length or a file's host path — a file input holds no text editor, so its reading is its `value` attribute, which still holds the chosen file's host path in the DOM and in form submission, outside the snapshot —, `selected`, `pressed` and `invalid` the accessibility node's own, read at the one construction site and never parsed a second time from the element — `selected` its `is_selected()`, `pressed` its `toggled()` off the five checkable roles, with only `Toggled::True` reading `Some(true)` and both `False` and `Mixed` reading `Some(false)`, `invalid` its `invalid().is_some()` — a boolean model with two limits, a mixed toggle reading not pressed and a grammar or spelling error reading invalid, the node keeping the full value; the three are what the engine's builder writes from `aria-selected`, `aria-pressed` (or `aria-checked` on a checkable role) and `aria-invalid` (§Standard Contracts → Mutation, query and CSSOM)
 — a select's option's `selected` its chosen state, so a choice names the old and the new option with `selected` in `differs`, and on the stand each reading is asserted equal to its accessibility node's, in both layout modes: exactly the chosen flight type's option reads selected, exactly the selected CRUD row reads selected, and a date field reads invalid while what it holds is no date — the stand states no `aria-pressed`, the flight booker's mode a `select#flight-type` whose options state its choice, and `accessibility_states` pins the pressed reading on a fixture (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:178-183; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:60-87; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:367-496 — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-snapshot-states/report.md, the flight type's at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-25-cold-agent-bar/report.md) —, `focused` the `TreeUpdate`'s `focus` (never `get_focussed_node_id`, which falls back to the root element) — and no field holds a `NodeId`, an AccessKit tree id, an `ElementId`, a `ScopeId` or a pointer;
 the snapshot has one serialized form, the text `Snapshot::to_text` returns (the next clause), and one driver command returns that text — `snapshot`, run through `escher_driver::Session::run` — to the code that called it in process or, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, across the session socket to the `escher-session` command line, which writes it as the `text` field of one line of JSON on stdout (with `part` and `parts` beside it when the screen is read in parts), and since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface to an MCP client as the `snapshot` tool's result, the screen text itself — a paged one its JSON line `{"text","part","parts"}` —, on the `escher-session mcp` role's stdout (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:11-77; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:96-115; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:127-285; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/lib.rs:34-38; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot.rs:1-5; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_snapshot_state.rs:1-11)
 — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-snapshot-model/report.md, the password mask and the pinned `enabled` reading at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-snapshot-state-fidelity/report.md, the file-input mask at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-compact-snapshot-serialization/report.md; under the same feature `Snapshot::to_text(&self) -> String`, an inherent method in the crate-private module `snapshot_text`, is the snapshot's one text form — a pure function of the `Snapshot` (no document access, no failure path, no log, no print): one line per node in the pre-order of `Snapshot::nodes()`, each ended by a line break, a child indented two spaces deeper than its parent, a snapshot with no roots the empty string; a line reads the role in its `Debug` spelling (no alias table), the name as a quoted string, `id=` and the id quoted, the state tokens the model holds in the fixed order `enabled` / `disabled` · `checked` / `unchecked` · `value=` with the value quoted · `selected` / `unselected` · `pressed` / `unpressed` · `invalid` · `focused` (a token absent where the model holds nothing for it; `invalid` written only when true; the three after `value=` since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states — packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot_text.rs:112-124), then `@{x},{y} {width}x{height}` with each number in `f64`'s `Display` form (`TextInput "Name:" id="who" enabled value="Ada" focused @8,8 200x24`); a quoted string is written in `str`'s `Debug` form, so it never holds a line break or a bare `"`, and an apostrophe and printable non-ASCII are written as they are; there is no `Display` impl, no second entry point, no parser of the text, no JSON form, and `to_text` itself never truncates or pages;
 beside it `Snapshot::text_parts(&self, budget: usize) -> Vec<TextPart>` (`TextPart { text: String, ids: Vec<String> }`, `Debug` · `Clone` · `Default` · `PartialEq` · `Eq`) cuts that text into parts — consecutive pre-order lines while a part stays within `budget` bytes, never splitting a line, a line longer than `budget` a part alone, an empty snapshot one empty part — the parts concatenated being `to_text()`, the two sharing one private pre-order walk, with no document access, failure path, log or print (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot_text.rs:59-81); the public constant `SNAPSHOT_TEXT_BUDGET: usize = 10_000` is the ceiling one screen's text stays under, in bytes of `to_text`'s result — at most as many characters and at most as many tokens, so inside the agent client's documented 10,000-token warning, 25,000-token maximum and 50,000-character file threshold — a ceiling a caller compares against, never enforced by `to_text`, `text_parts` the reader that cuts the text within it, and it is re-exported, with `TextPart`, from the crate and through dioxus-native's `pub use dioxus_native_dom::*`; the text leaves the process through the returned value and, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, in a hosted `snapshot`'s answer — over the session socket and onto the command line's stdout (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-10; until then the returned value was its only exit, ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07) — and no log or event carries the snapshot or its text, while a kept check holds it at rest — each kept answer whole, a `snapshot`'s text and an acting verb's diff included — in an owner-only file never logged, the two committed checks under `tests/blitz-tests/checks/` the one exception to owner-only;
